<title>ITALY: FORECAST-Italy mkt still expects small rate easing.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Italy mkt still expects small rate easing.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's money market still expects a slight rate cut, a study based on implicit forward rates by the Bocconi University's research arm Igier showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The study showed the implicit overnight rate standing in one month's time at 8.54 percent from the actual level of 8.63 percent on Thursday, the day on which Igier based its study.</p>
<p>One week ago the implicit overnight rate was seen standing at 8.51 percent, while one month ago it was seen at 8.83 percent.</p>
<p>On a three month horizon the implicit overnight rate is seen standing at 8.42 percent, while one week ago it was seen at 8.43 oercent. On a one year horizon the implicit overnight rate is seen at 8.31 percent.</p>
<p>The spread between the implied Italian overnight rate and the implied German overnight rate in two years' time, seen as a good indicator of market confidence in Europe's Economic and Monetary Union, is seen at 332 basis points from 336 basis points one week ago and 305 bps one month ago.</p>
